---
const interests = ["AI experimentation", "AI news & podcasts", "Information security", "Swimming", "Cycling"];
const languages = ["Ukrainian", "English", "Polish"];
---

<section id="beyond-work" class="mesh-bg px-6 py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-5 md:gap-16">
    <div class="reveal md:col-span-3">
      <h2 class="eyebrow text-xs font-semibold uppercase text-[#a9791f] mb-3">Beyond Work</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        I read across three languages — Ukrainian, English, and Polish —
        mostly for the range of perspective it brings; each language surfaces
        different sources, framing, and depth on the same topics.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        I keep a daily habit of AI news and information security podcasts
        alongside books and articles in both spaces, which keeps me current on
        a field that shifts weekly.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">
        I actively experiment with AI — both in domains I already know deeply
        (to sharpen judgment on where it genuinely helps vs. where it doesn't)
        and in new areas entirely, using it to compress the learning curve and
        get to competence faster than I could unassisted.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[#5b6472] leading-relaxed">Outside of screens: swimming and cycling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal md:col-span-2 content-start">
      <h4 class="text-sm text-[#5b6472] mb-4">Languages</h4>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-8">
        {languages.map((lang) => (
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#d4d9e2] bg-white px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-[#111827]">
            {lang}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h4 class="text-sm text-[#5b6472] mb-4">Interests</h4>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        {interests.map((item) => (
          <span class="rounded-full border border-[#d4d9e2] bg-white px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-[#111827]">
            {item}
          </span>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
